  "test": "published-artifacts-and-permanent-cluster-wide-argocd-upgrade",
  "note": "Verified after actual crates.io, GitHub and GHCR publication. Every public asset and both Cargo archives match reviewed exact-tag bytes. All native indexes are public, and the globally Cargo-installed CLI verifies automatic catalog fetching before an isolated configuration refusal without a Kubernetes endpoint. The permanent four-node mixed cluster upgrades from the public 0.6.0 chart to the public 0.6.1 chart through Argo CD, using built-in pins without overrides. Fresh unknown, AMD64 and ARM64 placements run before and after the upgrade. Original installation/volume identities, 247 pre-upgrade release contracts, nine credential identities/bytes and administrator policy remain intact. Shared schema 6 and all CRD identities/definitions stay unchanged. Complete authenticated readback verifies 18 historical, 35 frozen-input and 18 fresh placement graphs. Historical metadata from retired backends is not claimed as verified registry bytes. CLI/Helm/Argo fixture interruptions, rollbacks and removals are recorded separately before publication with byte-identical candidate images/chart. The permanent installation is not uninstalled, downgraded or interrupted, and shared Nodes stay unchanged. Initial site hashes precede the receipt documentation update. Private node names, kubeconfig context, credential material and infrastructure repository details are omitted.",
